{"response":{"docs":[{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03310073","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03310073","description":["SIREN DB annotation:\n* finely ground FOODON:03430106\n* not heat-treated FOODON:03440003\n* starch FOODON:03420203\n* water removal process FOODON:03460138\n* preservation by dehydration or drying FOODON:03470116"],"label":"rice starch","obo_id":"FOODON:03310073","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://opendata.inrae.fr/PO2/Ontology/TransformON/c_S8Nvm9","ontology_name":"tfo","ontology_prefix":"TFO","short_form":"c_S8Nvm9","description":[],"label":"rice starch","obo_id":"c_S8Nvm9","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/LFID_0006283","ontology_name":"lifestylefactors","ontology_prefix":"LIFESTYLEFACTORS","short_form":"LFID_0006283","description":[],"label":"rice starch","obo_id":"LFID:0006283","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_753027","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["Amylum oryzae","Oryza sativa (rice) starch","Oryza sativa starch","Rice starch","Starch, rice"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_753027","description":[],"label":"starch, rice","obo_id":"CHEBI:753027","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C80780","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C80780","description":[],"label":"Starch, Rice","obo_id":"NCIT:C80780","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["STARCH, RICE","Starch, Rice"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03544165","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03544165","description":["The group includes any type of rice starch, excluding modified starch, that is listed among additives, according to the EU regulation. The part consumed/analysed is by default the whole or a portion of it representing the observed heterogeneity. ] and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starches] and [https://www.google.co.uk/search?tbm\u003disch\u0026q\u003dRice starch]"],"label":"41650 - rice starch (efsa foodex2)","obo_id":"FOODON:03544165","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00002208","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_00002208","description":[],"label":"rice starch refined food product","obo_id":"FOODON:00002208","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/C000612720","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["SSG6 protein, Oryza sativa","SSG6 protein, rice","aminotransferase ACS12, rice"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_C000612720","description":[],"label":"substandard starch grain6 protein, rice","obo_id":"mesh:C000612720","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D005433","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["Almond Flour","Almond Flours","Almond Meal","Almond Meals","Corn Flour","Corn Flours","Corn Meal","Corn Meals","Flour, Almond","Flour, Corn","Flour, Grain","Flour, Nut","Flour, Potato","Flour, Rice","Flour, Semolina","Flour, Soybean","Flour, Wheat","Flours","Flours, Almond","Flours, Corn","Flours, Grain","Flours, Nut","Flours, Potato","Flours, Rice","Flours, Semolina","Flours, Soybean","Flours, Wheat","Grain Flour","Grain Flours","Grain Meal","Grain Meals","Meal, Almond","Meal, Corn","Meal, Grain","Meal, Rice","Meal, Soybean","Meal, Wheat","Meals, Almond","Meals, Corn","Meals, Grain","Meals, Rice","Meals, Soybean","Meals, Wheat","Nut Flour","Nut Flours","Potato Flour","Potato Flours","Rice Flour","Rice Flours","Rice Meal","Rice Meals","Semolina Flour","Semolina Flours","Soybean Flour","Soybean Flours","Soybean Meal","Soybean Meals","Wheat Flour","Wheat Flours","Wheat Meal","Wheat Meals"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_D005433","description":["A powdery meal obtained from ground up starchy foodstuff, such as seeds of WHEAT; RICE and other EDIBLE GRAIN; LEGUMES; and NUTS; or ground up PLANT TUBERS."],"label":"Flour","obo_id":"mesh:D005433","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00002575","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_00002575","description":["An Italian short-grain rice.","It is named after the town of Arborio, in the Po Valley, which is situated in the main growing region of Doron. Arborio is also grown in Arkansas, California, and Missouri in the United States. When cooked, the rounded grains are firm, and creamy and chewy compared to other rices, due to their higher amylopectin starch content."],"label":"Arborio rice","obo_id":"FOODON:00002575","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03400813","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03400813","description":["Examples: wheat flour, wholemeal, substitute flours and starches, wheat flour, patent, soya flour, rye flour, whole, potato flour, cornflour, carob flour, rice flour, arrowroot, buckwheat flour, tapioca","LanguaL curation note: Renamed from *FLOUR OR STARCH (EUROFIR)* (LanguaL 2010)."],"label":"cereal or cereal-like milling products and derivatives (eurofir)","obo_id":"FOODON:03400813","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00004353","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_00004353","description":["A long grain white rice endosperm that has a low amylose starch content."],"label":"white glutinous rice","obo_id":"FOODON:00004353","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C97919","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C97919","description":["A paste containing multiple skin protectants with anti-oxidant, skin protecting, moisturizing, anti-erythema and anti-inflammatory activities. The paste includes zinc oxide, aluminum starch octenylsuccinate, lanolin, allantoin, chamomile and sweet almond oil, rice bran oil, shea butter, dimethicone (polymerized siloxane), petrolatum, vitamin E, phytosome of glycyrrhetinic acid and botanical extracts derived from Calendula officinalis, Malva sylvestris and Tilia tomentosa. Upon application, this paste provides a physical barrier on the skin and may help protect, soothe and moisturize the skin as well as restore skin softness, integrity and elasticity. When this paste is applied to the perineum area, it may help prevent radiation-induced dermatitis."],"label":"Zinc Oxide/Aluminum Starch Octenylsuccinate/Glycyrrhetinic Phytosome/Vitamin E/Botanical Extracts-Based Skin Protectant Paste","obo_id":"NCIT:C97919","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["Alkagin","Zinc Oxide/Aluminum Starch Octenylsuccinate/Glycyrrhetinic Phytosome/Vitamin E/Botanical Extracts-Based Skin Protectant Paste"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03307722","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03307722","description":["SIREN DB annotation:\n* liquid, high viscosity, with no visible particles FOODON:03430139\n* starch FOODON:03420203\n* water removal process FOODON:03460138"],"label":"rice syrup","obo_id":"FOODON:03307722","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03309985","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03309985","description":["SIREN DB annotation:\n* whole, shape achieved by forming FOODON:03430147\n* partially heat-treated FOODON:03440018\n* starch FOODON:03420203\n* pasteurization by heating FOODON:03470135"],"label":"rice cake","obo_id":"FOODON:03309985","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420133","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03420133","description":["LanguaL curation note: In the case of grains (NT of *GRAIN [B1324]*), the descriptor can be used to describe whole grains, which may include  may include amaranth, barley, buckwheat, bulgur, corn (including popcorn), millet, quinoa, rice, rye, oats, sorghum, teff, triticale, wheat, and wild rice.*\nRenamed from *SEED OR KERNEL, SKIN PRESENT, GERM PRESENT* in LanguaL 2008.","Whole grains are cereal grains (NT of *GRAIN [B1324]*) that consist of the intact, ground, cracked or flaked caryopsis, whose principal anatomical components - the starchy endosperm, germ and bran - are present in the same relative proportions as they exist in the intact caryopsis - should be considered a whole grain food.\nThis definition means that 100% of the original kernel all of the bran, germ, and endosperm must be present to qualify as a whole grain.\nWhole grains or foods made from them contain all the essential parts and naturally-occurring nutrients of the entire grain seed. If the grain has been processed (e.g., cracked, crushed, rolled, extruded, and/or cooked), the food product should deliver approximately the same rich balance of nutrients that are found in the original grain seed.[http://www.fda.gov/Food/GuidanceComplianceRegulatoryInformation/GuidanceDocuments/FoodLabelingNutrition/ucm059088.htm]"],"label":"seed, skin present, germ present","obo_id":"FOODON:03420133","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_753027","ontology_name":"dron","related_synonyms":["Amylum oryzae","Oryza sativa (rice) starch","Oryza sativa starch","Rice starch","Starch, rice"],"ontology_prefix":"DRON","short_form":"CHEBI_753027","description":[],"label":"starch, rice","obo_id":"CHEBI:753027","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_753027","ontology_name":"slm","related_synonyms":["Amylum oryzae","Oryza sativa (rice) starch","Oryza sativa starch","Rice starch","Starch, rice"],"ontology_prefix":"SLM","short_form":"CHEBI_753027","description":[],"label":"starch, rice","obo_id":"","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420133","ontology_name":"ecto","ontology_prefix":"ECTO","short_form":"FOODON_03420133","description":["LanguaL curation note: In the case of grains (NT of *GRAIN [B1324]*), the descriptor can be used to describe whole grains, which may include  may include amaranth, barley, buckwheat, bulgur, corn (including popcorn), millet, quinoa, rice, rye, oats, sorghum, teff, triticale, wheat, and wild rice.*\nRenamed from *SEED OR KERNEL, SKIN PRESENT, GERM PRESENT* in LanguaL 2008.","Whole grains are cereal grains (NT of *GRAIN [B1324]*) that consist of the intact, ground, cracked or flaked caryopsis, whose principal anatomical components - the starchy endosperm, germ and bran - are present in the same relative proportions as they exist in the intact caryopsis - should be considered a whole grain food.\nThis definition means that 100% of the original kernel all of the bran, germ, and endosperm must be present to qualify as a whole grain.\nWhole grains or foods made from them contain all the essential parts and naturally-occurring nutrients of the entire grain seed. If the grain has been processed (e.g., cracked, crushed, rolled, extruded, and/or cooked), the food product should deliver approximately the same rich balance of nutrients that are found in the original grain seed.[http://www.fda.gov/Food/GuidanceComplianceRegulatoryInformation/GuidanceDocuments/FoodLabelingNutrition/ucm059088.htm]"],"label":"seed, skin present, germ present","obo_id":"FOODON:03420133","type":"class"}],"numFound":19,"start":0},"responseHeader":{"QTime":0,"status":0},"facet_counts":{"facet_fields":{"ontologyPreferredPrefix":["FOODON","9","mesh","2","NCIT","2","ECTO","1","LIFESTYLEFACTORS","1","","1","TFO","1","CHEBI","1","DRON","1"],"isDefiningOntology":["true","15","false","4"],"ontologyId":["foodon","9","ncit","2","mesh","2","lifestylefactors","1","slm","1","chebi","1","tfo","1","dron","1","ecto","1"],"ontologyIri":["http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/foodon.owl","9","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ncit.owl","2","https://w3id.org/biopragmatics/resources/mesh/mesh.ofn","2","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/dron.owl","1","","1","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/TEMP.owl","1","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ecto.owl","1","http://opendata.inrae.fr/PO2/Ontology/TransformON/","1","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/chebi.owl","1"],"isObsolete":["false","19","true","1"],"type":["class","19"]}}}